-- title:
--   Gauss ring restricted to L(j) is a discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be any subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ which is assumed to equal [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb Q \to L$ of the elements of the $\mathbb Q$-subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb Q\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb Q\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain with $L$ as its fraction field, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that of $L$. Let $j \in K$ be an element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq} = q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$, and assume $j \neq 0$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ whose membership is given by Gauss presentations over $A$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ (coefficients pushed forward along $A \to L$). Then there exists a valuation subring $O_E$ of the intermediate field $L(j) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin L {j}` inside $K$ such that: $O_E$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $e \in L(j)$ one has $e \in O_E$ if and only if $e \in W_0$ as an element of $K$; $e \in O_E$ if and only if there are polynomials $P, Q \in A[X]$ with the reduction of $Q$ modulo the maximal ideal nonzero and $e \cdot Q(j) = P(j)$ in $K$; whenever $e, P, Q$ satisfy these two conditions, $e$ is a non-unit of $O_E$ exactly when the reduction of $P$ is zero; and for every irreducible $\varpi \in A$ there is an irreducible element of $O_E$ whose image in $K$ is $\varpi$, so that $A \to O_E$ is unramified of ramification index one.
--
--   This identifies the restriction to $L(j)$ of the Gauss valuation ring of $L\cdot\mathbb Q(X(\Gamma)) \subseteq L((q))$ as a discrete valuation ring, with membership and non-units read off from presentations $e\,Q(j) = P(j)$ with $A$-polynomial coefficients. It supplies the base discrete valuation ring over which the fundamental identity $\sum_i e_i f_i = [F:E]$ is applied in the study of Igusa valuations and Drinfeld charts on modular curves, and is cited by the statements bounding and describing those valuations.
